        "original_id": "ec0e894b-477a-5e73-945b-788b6422ca72",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Amy Lee, Jimi Hendrix, Dave Eggar, Dave Fortman\n- Organizations: Evanescence\n- Works: War Story, Voice from the Stone, Good Enough\n- Roles: singer, songwriter, record producer, multi-instrumentalist, electric guitarist, producer\n\nFacts:\n- Amy Lynn Hartzler, née Lee, was born on December 13, 1981, and is professionally known as Amy Lee.\n- Amy Lee is an American singer, songwriter, record producer, and multi-instrumentalist.\n- Jimi Hendrix's mainstream career lasted only four years.\n- Jimi Hendrix is widely regarded as one of the most influential electric guitarists in the history of popular music and one of the most celebrated musicians of the 20th century.\n- During Evanescence's hiatus, Amy Lee began a film score career in 2013.\n- Amy Lee composed the soundtrack for the 2014 film War Story with cellist Dave Eggar.\n- Amy Lee composed music for a 2015 work with Dave Eggar, but the title is blank in the source text.\n- Amy Lee wrote the song \"Speak to Me\" for the film Voice from the Stone.\n- The Evanescence song \"Good Enough\" was written by lead vocalist Amy Lee.\n- \"Good Enough\" was produced by Dave Fortman.",
